long_rate 120->70bp, real_rate 100->65bp, credit_spread 60->45bp. Phi and the
innovation correlations untouched. Diagnosed, not assumed: the level term was
106% of LongGovt variance and the annual-change sd of an AR(1) is ~1.05 sigma
at phi=0.80, so persistence was never the lever.

LongGovt 22.7% -> 14.3%, ILG 18.9% -> 13.3%, IG_Credit 9.8% -> 7.7%. Equity
block unchanged. V-M4 floor binding 10.1% -> 7.1% as a by-product.

Re-run attribution (5 seeds) and CGB dial (3 seeds) via the new
tools/rerun_multiseed.py: re-anchor +101.6k / +82.5k (unchanged within noise
vs the post-V-C3 article figures), bond-side +30.5k / +45.2k (unchanged), China
cap now +4k in both worlds, pot levels down ~6% (convexity windfall removed).

V-M7 re-measured: no longer a symptom of V-M3. The repress() boundary inflates
repression-leg levels by ~8% (ramp sensitivity in the report). Recommended,
not implemented. V-D7 added. Three tests added; 46/46.

Also untracks simple_alm_changes.zip (was re-added in ee985aa).
